{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791663490,"nonce":"s5OGofjxrJzn5U5RNYYKMgxsFgY=","title":"Mail alerts: LinkedIn job alert emails parser and resolution","message":"User is subscribing to LinkedIn job alerts. Add a mailalerts parser for LinkedIn job alert emails (and single-job recommendation emails): title, company, location, workplace type, posted age, salary if shown, and the LinkedIn job id from linkedin.com/comm/jobs/view/\u003cid\u003e links (strip tracking params). Never fetch linkedin.com: its robots.txt disallows generic crawlers and its terms forbid scraping (specs/008). Resolve instead by (1) matching existing ingested jobs by employer+title+location and merging, (2) if the employer's ATS is known via ats_rules/apply_link history, looking the posting up through that ATS's public board API through FetchContext, else (3) keeping it as an email-manual group with a partial description and a Paste full description prompt (as other alert sources do). Never auto-score email-manual groups unless the existing rules allow. Needs real samples: after the user subscribes, run jobhunter mail sample for LinkedIn senders and save scrubbed fixtures (no addresses, no names). Related: 048a6a0.","files":null}]}